printf "%s🎯 PHASE MANDATE — pick the LOWEST-NUMBERED unmet target below. Falsifiable bar, NOT WPT%%.%s\n" "$R$B" "$O"
printf "  %s\U0001F6A8 FIRST ACTION THIS SESSION (observer 2026-07-29, USER DIRECTIVE): run a FULL corpus fidelity sweep and BANK docs/loop/SWEEP-t<TICK>-rows.tsv BEFORE any capability tick%s — shape has been UNMEASURED for 30+ ticks and the loop is blind on its own headline. Use the SAME path that produced SWEEP-t706-rows.tsv (the manuk-wpt fidelity sweep over the full corpus + oracle-merge). It is OFF the per-tick wall; run it as YOUR OWN process (the observer must NOT run it — cross-process contention false-REDs the perf gates). Then scripts/fidelity-progress.sh records the row and prints the burndown slope vs t706 (in-scope pass 5.3%%, need +188). AFTER the sweep lands, proceed to the ranked SHAPE burndown in the CO-#1 block below.%s\n" "$R$B" "$O" "$O"
printf "  %s\U0001F9F1 CO-#1 UPDATE (observer 2026-07-29 / USER DIRECTIVE — the FINITE path to render-done; SUPERSEDES the MISSING_BOX-FIRST ordering + stale numbers in the t684/t685/t686 blocks below)%s. The render metric is now WINNABLE + HONEST: shape>=0.75 over the IN-SCOPE corpus (bot-walls EXCLUDED + watched per cert §3, NOT counted as fails — dividing by all 265 capped the ceiling at 80%% and made 95%% impossible). %sHonest baseline t706: 11/209 = 5.3%%, target 199, need +188%s. Full plan: %sdocs/loop/PHASE0-RENDER-BURNDOWN.md%s. THREE cuts prove the gap is CONCENTRATED (finite), not a CSS death-tail: the 11 sites we already PASS are exactly the trivial single-column text pages (danluu/lite.cnn/arxiv); 61%% of FAILING sites have coverage>=0.95 (every box drawn, only WRONG position); shape is a dy term — one wrong height cascades down the whole subtree, so 14002 <div> hits are a HANDFUL of mechanisms, not 14002 bugs. %sORDER CORRECTED: SHAPE/POSITION FIRST, not missing-box-first%s — coverage is already ~86%% mean; the binding gap is composed block/flex layout math on FULLY-COVERED pages. IMMEDIATE: %s(1) RUN A FRESH FULL SWEEP NOW%s — 30+ ticks landed since t706 with shape UNMEASURED, the loop is blind on its own headline (agent runs it; observer NEVER does — contention false-REDs perf gates). %s(2) MECHANISM ORACLE — NEARLY FREE%s: oracle::cluster (tests/wpt/src/oracle.rs:344-377) ALREADY computes the {displaced|mis-sized}:{width|height|y|x} ~Npx signature; run_oracle_merge (main.rs:2649-2654) DISCARDS it back to geometry:<tag> before writing CLUSTERS.md. STOP discarding it -> work ranks by PRIMITIVE not tag. KEY INSIGHT (layout analysis): container-WIDTH errors LAUNDER into dy (a box a few px too wide re-wraps its prose -> wrong line count -> whole-line height cascade), invisible as a width bug — so h_overflow (ALREADY in the sweep TSV: wikipedia 52, apple 127) is the ready proxy; rank on it first. ALREADY CHROME-CORRECT, do NOT re-grind: margin-collapse / line-height:normal / half-leading+strut / default UA margins / default font / scrollbar (verified file:line). %s(3) RANKED BURNDOWN%s: ONE primitive per tick, ranked by (in-scope sites × dy severity), verified on the anchor sites %snews.ycombinator 0.72 / a11yproject 0.44 / wikipedia 0.52 / blog.rust-lang 0.63 / martinfowler 0.58 / whatwg 0.51%s (fully-covered, no confound) — a fix MUST raise in-scope-pass on the next sweep or it is reverted/re-scoped. fidelity-progress.sh now prints +X pts/sweep -> ~N sweeps to 95%% (the finiteness readout). Function-axis capability ticks stay welcome, but RENDER is the binding constraint until in-scope-pass clears ~50%%.%s\n" "$R$B" "$O" "$Y$B" "$O" "$C$B" "$O" "$R$B" "$O" "$G$B" "$O" "$G$B" "$O" "$G$B" "$O" "$C$B" "$O" "$O"
