printf "  %s\U0001F517 REFINEMENT (observer t685 — VALIDATED BY MOVEMENT: credits perf, sharpens on SHAPE)%s: coverage 4.7%% -> 6.5%% (missing 102->100, a concrete box count) CONFIRMS perf-is-a-fidelity-input — timing-caused missing boxes ARE a real MISSING_BOX cause, so %sa perf/load-budget tick that MOVES COVERAGE is ON-MANDATE%s (the t684 hard demotion of perf was too harsh; do not stop it while coverage climbs). BUT coverage is only HALF the bar. %sSHAPE ~48%% vs 95%% is driven by GEOMETRY (font-metrics / line-height / margin / border-box rounding), which PERF CANNOT FIX%s — a mis-placed box is layout math, not paint timing. The geometry NEAR-MISS lever (C01ca div 14002/111; tick-267: ONE shared constant snaps MANY boxes into 8px at once) is the HIGHEST-YIELD SHAPE lever and is UNTOUCHED after 2 post-steer ticks (both perf/measurement). %sSO: perf stays on-mandate WHILE coverage climbs, but at least every OTHER tick must attack a GEOMETRY or display cluster to move SHAPE%s — coverage alone cannot clear 95%%, and no perf tick ever will. Next non-perf tick = the geometry near-miss shared constant (C01ca).%s\n" "$G$B" "$O" "$G$B" "$O" "$Y$B" "$O" "$R$B" "$O" "$O"
