printf "  %s\U0001F3C1 CURRENT ORDERS (observer, tick ~543 / 2026-07-24 — SUPERSEDES every steer below where they conflict)%s. The capability count FEELS near-done, but the Phase-0 CERTIFICATE has NOT been measured with the rebuilt instrument — the last real jarring numbers are the t380->t392 sweep, STALE by ~150 ticks + the whole instrument rebuild (t531-537). Feeling done is not being done; that is exactly what the instrument exists to catch. %sSTEP 1 — RUN THE EXIT VERIFICATION NOW (Tier-3, top priority, ~5-10 ticks)%s: (a) a FRESH full-corpus sweep with the rebuilt G1 instrument (SHAPE + selector-path keying + all four jarring invariants, bricks t531-537) — append one actuals line to PHASE0-ROADMAP-ANCHOR.md; (b) run test262 (SpiderMonkey embedded, near-zero cost, number unknown); (c) run the 100-tab RSS benchmark. This converts near-done into a NUMBER and tells us the real distance to the certificate. %sSTEP 2 — FINISH THE IN-SCOPE BOUNDED REMAINDER (everything in PHASE0-BOUNDED-REMAINDER.md Tier-1/Tier-2 that is NOT the death-tail), re-probing each first (rows run stale-PESSIMISTIC)%s: password vault + autofill (crypto core done in store/lib.rs, the iceberg is UX), live CSS transition/animation timeline (end-state-only today), the visual-effects bundle (filter / backdrop-filter / mix-blend-mode / clip-path / background-attachment), form-widget painting (date/color/time pickers, native select popup, accent-color), cookie-attribute enforcement, bidi full line reordering, WebAuthn full round-trip, codec-breadth completion, multicol, print output — plus ANYTHING the fresh sweep flags as jarring. %sDEATH-TAIL — do NOT build; feature-detect cleanly and NAME as post-Phase-0 exceptions%s: the 16-item cut line (Widevine/WebRTC/WebTransport-HTTP3/SharedWorker/canvas-office EDITING/in-browser-PDF/devtools/process-per-tab/Web-Audio/push) PLUS subgrid, @scope, anchor-positioning, JPEG XL, WebCodecs, scroll-driven animations, custom highlights, text-wrap:balance, JSPI, scop